# LAMMPS script for Cu NPT equilibration followed by 20% tensile deformation along x
# Material: copper (fcc), lattice constant 3.615 Å
# Temperature: 300 K, Pressure: 0 bar during equilibration
# Deformation: 20% engineering strain in 200 ps
# Note: strain rate is set to 0.001 /ps (0.2/200) to achieve 20% stretch.
# If you prefer 1e-5 /ps, increase run to 2,000,000 steps (20,000 ps).

units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p

variable T equal 300.0
variable P equal 0.0

# Lattice and region (10x10x10 fcc unit cells -> ~4000 atoms)
lattice fcc 3.615
Lattice spacing in x,y,z = 3.615 3.615 3.615
region box block 0 36.15 0 36.15 0 36.15 units box
create_box 1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (36.15 36.15 36.15)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
create_atoms 1 box
Created 4000 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (36.15 36.15 36.15)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.000 seconds

# Interatomic potential (EAM for Cu)
pair_style eam
pair_coeff * * Cu_u3.eam
Reading eam potential file Cu_u3.eam with DATE: 2007-06-11

# Initial velocities
velocity all create ${T} 87287
velocity all create 300 87287

# ===== NPT Equilibration =====
fix fxnpt all npt temp ${T} ${T} 0.1 iso ${P} ${P} 1.0
fix fxnpt all npt temp 300 ${T} 0.1 iso ${P} ${P} 1.0
fix fxnpt all npt temp 300 300 0.1 iso ${P} ${P} 1.0
fix fxnpt all npt temp 300 300 0.1 iso 0 ${P} 1.0
fix fxnpt all npt temp 300 300 0.1 iso 0 0 1.0
thermo 1000
thermo_style custom step temp pe ke etotal press vol lx ly lz density
dump d1 all custom 500 dump.equil.lammpstrj id type x y z
run 0   # 50 ps equilibration
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 1 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 6.95
  ghost atom cutoff = 6.95
  binsize = 3.475, bins = 11 11 11
  1 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 1 0 0
  (1) pair eam, perpetual
      attributes: half, newton on
      pair build: half/bin/atomonly/newton
      stencil: half/bin/3d
      bin: standard
